  - Inputs need [38;5;153mname[39m attributes. Today's form has only [38;5;153mid[39ms, so [38;5;153mname="username"[39m and [38;5;153mname="password"[39m get added.
  - Error text goes into an element marked [38;5;153mdata-error-for="<field>"[39m. The binder sets [38;5;153mtextContent[39m there and toggles
    [38;5;153maria-invalid[39m on the input. If no such element exists for a field, it skips rendering rather than throwing — a
    missing error slot shouldn't break submission.

  Every submit clears all previous errors first, so stale messages can't linger.

  [1mIntegration.[0m [38;5;153mapp.js[39m loses [38;5;153mvalidateForm()[39m and its hand-rolled submit handler, and gains a rules object plus one
  [38;5;153mbindForm[39m call. [38;5;153mlogin()[39m and [38;5;153mAPI_ENDPOINT[39m are untouched — this change doesn't go near the login stub. [38;5;153mindex.html[39m
  switches to [38;5;153m<script type="module">[39m and gains the [38;5;153mname[39m attributes and two error spans.

  [1mWhat gets tested.[0m The core is pure, so [38;5;153mvalidate[39m and each built-in validator get real unit tests — empty values,
  boundary lengths, cross-field access via the second argument, and the first-failure-wins ordering. The binder needs a
  DOM, so I'd cover it by asserting the pieces that don't: field extraction and error application as separate exported
  functions. I'm not proposing a headless-browser setup for a four-field app.

  [1mTooling.[0m The repo currently has no test runner, no linter, and zero dependencies. Cheapest moment to fix that is now,
  before the code exists:

